PicoRV32 SoC for Tang Nano 20K
================================

This project targets only the Sipeed Tang Nano 20K (GW2AR-LV18QN88C8/I7).
The PicoRV32 system clock is 27 MHz.  Firmware is embedded in the FPGA
bitstream through the SRAM initialization files in src/.

The application configures a Hi-Link LD2450 radar for multi-target mode,
reads all three target records through a dedicated 256000-baud UART, and
prints X/Y coordinates, speed, and distance resolution through the board's
USB UART at 115200 baud.

Build firmware first:

    cd c_code
    make clean
    make

Then open picorv32_20k.gprj in Gowin EDA and run a full build.  The verified
bitstream is impl/pnr/picorv32_20k.fs.  See LD2450_README.md for wiring and
the radar MMIO register map.

Full SoC simulation
-------------------

After building the firmware, run this command from PowerShell:

    powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\sim\run_full_soc_testbench.ps1

The test runs the real PicoRV32 firmware, models the LD2450 configuration
ACKs and a three-target frame, checks the USB UART text, and checks the LED
target mask.  Success ends with:

    PASS: full PicoRV32 firmware + LD2450 three-target integration

Icarus may report that the mem_init files contain fewer than 8192 entries.
That is expected: the files contain the firmware image, while the unused
remainder of the 32 KiB SRAM does not need initialization for this test.
